.TH OROC-UPDATE 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.1" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-update \- Update tooling for manifests, signatures, and bundles.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc update <subcommand> [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Update tooling for manifests, signatures, and bundles.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBkeygen\fR
generate an Ed25519 keypair for update manifests
.TP
\fBinit\fR
scaffold a manifest JSON file
.TP
\fBserver\fR
run an update server over HTTP/TCP/UDP
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
query update servers or static manifests over HTTP/TCP/UDP
.TP
\fBsign\fR
sign a manifest JSON file and emit a sidecar signature
.TP
\fBverify\fR
verify a manifest JSON file + signature using a public key
.TP
\fBbundle\fR
build a tar archive from a directory suitable as an update artifact
.TP
\fBextract\fR
extract an update bundle tar archive into a directory
.TP
\fBvalidate\fR
validate a manifest.json file against the update manifest schema shape
.SH NOTES
.PP
All subcommands support '\-\-log\-file=<path>' to mirror logs to a JSON file. Advanced: set ORO_UPDATE_MANIFEST_FILENAME or pass '\-\-manifest\-name' on relevant subcommands to override the default manifest.json filename (and derived sidecar names).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc update init\fR
scaffold a default manifest.json in the current project
.TP
\fBoroc update bundle \-\-manifest manifest.json\fR
build a source bundle and record it in the manifest
.TP
\fBoroc update keygen > key.json\fR
generate a signing keypair JSON file
.TP
\fBoroc update sign \-\-keys key.json \-\-manifest manifest.json\fR
sign the manifest and write manifest.sig
.TP
\fBoroc update verify \-\-keys key.json \-\-manifest manifest.json\fR
verify manifest.json against manifest.sig with the public key
.TP
\fBoroc update server \-\-root ./updates\fR
run an HTTP update server serving manifests and bundles
.TP
\fBoroc update info \-\-http \-\-app\-id com.example.app \-\-follow\-manifest\fR
query an update server and fetch the referenced manifest
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
